1
00:00:02,336 --> 00:00:05,380
-[keyboard clattering]
-[gentle music]

2
00:00:21,355 --> 00:00:24,816
I hate it when we get
stuck on security duty.

3
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:29,029
Not me, because I
love to quash dissent.

4
00:00:29,112 --> 00:00:32,324
Sure, I love a bit of
dissent-quashing, too.

5
00:00:32,407 --> 00:00:34,701
Only problem,
there's never any dissent

6
00:00:34,785 --> 00:00:35,994
in the administration.

7
00:00:36,078 --> 00:00:37,663
[applicant yawns]

8
00:00:38,497 --> 00:00:41,792
-Was that a sigh of dissent?
-Huh?

9
00:00:41,875 --> 00:00:45,879
No, I'm just tired.
[yawns]

10
00:00:45,963 --> 00:00:49,216
You sure? Not a blatant call
to rally others against a system

11
00:00:49,299 --> 00:00:51,093
that treats you like
a cog in the machine,

12
00:00:51,176 --> 00:00:53,512
devaluing your
individuality and identity?

13
00:00:54,930 --> 00:00:56,807
No, it's fine, whatever.

14
00:00:56,890 --> 00:00:59,017
[sighs]
Guess there's just nothing out

15
00:00:59,101 --> 00:01:01,603
of the ordinary
going on around here.

16
00:01:02,646 --> 00:01:04,982
[upbeat music]

17
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:07,568
[keyboard clattering]

18
00:01:10,487 --> 00:01:12,281
[whooshing]

19
00:01:21,582 --> 00:01:22,708
[metal thuds]

20
00:01:27,629 --> 00:01:29,506
[vacuum whooshes]

21
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:31,800
[Arin grunts]

22
00:01:31,884 --> 00:01:32,926
[Sora grunts]

23
00:01:34,469 --> 00:01:35,929
Sorry.

24
00:01:37,556 --> 00:01:39,850
Empty?
Weird.

25
00:01:40,434 --> 00:01:42,269
[Sora] But perfect for
what we need.

26
00:01:45,898 --> 00:01:48,901
Man, our first
solo ninja mission.

27
00:01:48,984 --> 00:01:51,111
Just you and me,
like the old days.

28
00:01:51,195 --> 00:01:52,863
What's the deal
with this place again?

29
00:01:52,946 --> 00:01:55,866
Last time I was in here, the
agents said they find people

30
00:01:55,949 --> 00:01:58,285
that went missing during
the Merge and return them,

31
00:01:58,368 --> 00:02:01,705
but I think they were sending
people to the wrong places.

32
00:02:01,788 --> 00:02:03,874
If they found
my missing parents,

33
00:02:03,957 --> 00:02:05,584
they could've sent
them anywhere!

34
00:02:06,668 --> 00:02:08,962
Still, if the administration
is good at anything,

35
00:02:09,046 --> 00:02:10,547
it's record-keeping.

36
00:02:10,631 --> 00:02:12,174
They probably kept
notes of-- Hey!

37
00:02:12,257 --> 00:02:15,010
-[machine beeping]
-What's happening?

38
00:02:15,093 --> 00:02:16,720
Looks like the records
were taken offline

39
00:02:16,803 --> 00:02:19,515
when the head of the Department
of Realm Reassignment,

40
00:02:19,598 --> 00:02:22,142
some guy named Agent Walker,
went missing.

41
00:02:22,226 --> 00:02:25,437
[Arin] So info about my parents
could have been here,

42
00:02:25,521 --> 00:02:27,648
but I waited too long
to get it?

43
00:02:27,731 --> 00:02:30,150
[sighs] What's wrong with me?
I got distracted by ninja stuff.

44
00:02:30,234 --> 00:02:32,986
If you consider saving
the world a distraction.

45
00:02:33,070 --> 00:02:35,030
-[door thuds]
-[Agent Underwood] Yes, yes!

46
00:02:35,113 --> 00:02:37,407
Finally some dissent!

47
00:02:37,491 --> 00:02:39,201
It's quashing time!

48
00:02:40,536 --> 00:02:43,288
♪ Lost in the unknown
so much to see ♪

49
00:02:43,372 --> 00:02:46,375
♪ Together we will rise ♪

50
00:02:46,458 --> 00:02:49,545
♪ We fight ♪

51
00:02:49,628 --> 00:02:52,756
♪ Be a ninja for what's right ♪

52
00:02:54,091 --> 00:02:55,634
[flame roaring]

53
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:58,220
-[thud]
-[dragon roars]

54
00:03:08,230 --> 00:03:11,483
[gasps, sighs]

55
00:03:13,026 --> 00:03:14,945
-[Nya] Anything?
-[Lloyd] A lot,

56
00:03:15,028 --> 00:03:16,864
but not what I wanted to see.

57
00:03:16,947 --> 00:03:20,117
-Like where Ras' Dojo went?
-Exactly.

58
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:23,287
Master Rontu teaching me to
find harmony with my visions

59
00:03:23,370 --> 00:03:25,205
has been an enormous help,

60
00:03:25,289 --> 00:03:28,125
but that doesn't mean I can
make any sense of them.

61
00:03:28,208 --> 00:03:32,254
I saw Wolf Masks training,
but I have no idea where.

62
00:03:32,337 --> 00:03:34,214
Or who the
mysterious master was

63
00:03:34,298 --> 00:03:36,300
that Ras called out to
during the blood moon?

64
00:03:36,383 --> 00:03:39,178
What kind of being could
have that much power,

65
00:03:39,261 --> 00:03:41,722
to make an entire Dojo
disappear like that?

66
00:03:41,805 --> 00:03:44,141
No clue.
And until we figure it out,

67
00:03:44,224 --> 00:03:46,393
it's like we have no idea
what our next step should--

68
00:03:46,476 --> 00:03:48,770
-Whoa!
-[fire crackles]

69
00:03:48,854 --> 00:03:51,523
Playing through!
Kai once told me Boulder Golf

70
00:03:51,607 --> 00:03:55,402
would increase both
my power and accuracy.

71
00:03:55,485 --> 00:03:58,614
-Fore!
-[fire crackling]

72
00:04:02,117 --> 00:04:05,204
Wyldfyre's been
training non-stop since...

73
00:04:05,287 --> 00:04:08,707
Since my brave, stupid brother
got himself trapped forever

74
00:04:08,790 --> 00:04:09,958
in the Nether Space.

75
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:13,670
Wyldfyre's trying to live up to
what she thinks Kai would want.

76
00:04:13,754 --> 00:04:17,841
[Lloyd sighs] I know a thing or
two about thinking that way.

77
00:04:17,925 --> 00:04:20,427
But I'm worried she's putting
too much pressure on herself.

78
00:04:20,511 --> 00:04:23,305
Says the king of putting
too much pressure on himself.

79
00:04:23,388 --> 00:04:25,140
That's how I know it's bad.

80
00:04:25,224 --> 00:04:27,976
And she's not the only Ninja
trainee I'm worried about.

81
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:30,729
I expected to hear
from Arin or Sora by now.

82
00:04:30,812 --> 00:04:32,147
I'm sure they're fine.

83
00:04:33,398 --> 00:04:37,152
Agents, present arms!

84
00:04:37,236 --> 00:04:40,072
[Agent Underwood] You better
turn yourselves in, punks.

85
00:04:40,155 --> 00:04:44,159
We have blasters
and injunction paperwork,

86
00:04:44,243 --> 00:04:47,079
and we're not afraid
to use either!

87
00:04:47,162 --> 00:04:48,497
Better listen to her.

88
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:50,290
My partner's vicious
with her paperwork.

89
00:04:50,374 --> 00:04:53,919
She'll bury you
in 9-21Cs so hard,

90
00:04:54,002 --> 00:04:57,631
you'll wish you
51A-ed your 39-ZZ!

91
00:04:58,590 --> 00:05:00,342
I don't know what
any of that means,

92
00:05:00,425 --> 00:05:01,718
but we should be going.

93
00:05:04,263 --> 00:05:05,806
Hey, let go!

94
00:05:05,889 --> 00:05:07,307
Those are my favorite feet!

95
00:05:07,391 --> 00:05:09,268
[both thud]

96
00:05:09,351 --> 00:05:12,020
We can't get captured
on our first solo mission.

97
00:05:12,104 --> 00:05:15,274
Lloyd will never let us
out of the Monastery again!

98
00:05:15,357 --> 00:05:17,734
[gas hissing]

99
00:05:17,818 --> 00:05:19,403
[Agent Allen coughs]

100
00:05:19,486 --> 00:05:22,281
I bet that smoke bomb
isn't even licensed.

101
00:05:22,364 --> 00:05:24,449
Dispel the vapors!

102
00:05:26,869 --> 00:05:29,621
They've completely vanished!
Impossible!

103
00:05:29,705 --> 00:05:32,291
It must be some form of magic!

104
00:05:33,417 --> 00:05:35,460
[feet thudding]

105
00:05:48,098 --> 00:05:50,100
[growls]

106
00:05:53,770 --> 00:05:55,731
[laughs]
Great to see you too, Riyu,

107
00:05:55,814 --> 00:05:57,441
but we gotta move.

108
00:05:57,524 --> 00:05:59,443
They might figure out where
we went any second now.

109
00:05:59,526 --> 00:06:01,737
Seriously, where'd they go?

110
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:03,447
Oh, we'll never figure this out!

111
00:06:09,578 --> 00:06:12,372
[car engine roaring]

112
00:06:15,125 --> 00:06:17,544
Mission was a total fail, Riyu.

113
00:06:17,628 --> 00:06:21,131
If the administration had any
clues to where my parents are,

114
00:06:21,215 --> 00:06:22,716
those clues are gone now.

115
00:06:22,799 --> 00:06:24,468
It's okay, Arin.

116
00:06:24,551 --> 00:06:26,470
I'm sure we'll track them
down with some other lead.

117
00:06:26,553 --> 00:06:27,888
What other lead?

118
00:06:27,971 --> 00:06:31,141
-There is no--
-[Riyu roars]

119
00:06:31,225 --> 00:06:34,561
[car tires screech]

120
00:06:34,645 --> 00:06:35,854
[Matriarch thuds]

121
00:06:35,938 --> 00:06:37,898
What was that?

122
00:06:37,981 --> 00:06:39,816
We've got to check that out!

123
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:41,235
[car engine roaring]

124
00:06:41,318 --> 00:06:45,072
[thrilling music plays]

125
00:06:49,201 --> 00:06:50,953
[car tires screech]

126
00:06:51,036 --> 00:06:55,165
Whoa!
It's a dragon!

127
00:06:58,293 --> 00:07:00,921
[Riyu roars]

128
00:07:05,884 --> 00:07:08,595
It's the Matriarch of
the Mountain Dragons.

129
00:07:08,679 --> 00:07:10,681
Riyu's tribe mother.

130
00:07:10,764 --> 00:07:13,100
[emotional cries]

131
00:07:14,184 --> 00:07:16,770
[roars]

132
00:07:16,854 --> 00:07:19,231
[gasps]
Someone took her horns!

133
00:07:20,023 --> 00:07:21,525
[roars]

134
00:07:21,608 --> 00:07:24,945
We have to help her!

135
00:07:25,028 --> 00:07:27,155
I'll call the others on the
explorer's long-range comms.

136
00:07:27,239 --> 00:07:29,741
They'll take forever to
get all the way out here.

137
00:07:29,825 --> 00:07:31,952
The Matriarch needs help now.

138
00:07:32,035 --> 00:07:33,370
But what can we do?

139
00:07:33,453 --> 00:07:35,330
This is the Land of Madness.

140
00:07:35,414 --> 00:07:37,541
Riyu has a lot of friends here.

141
00:07:37,624 --> 00:07:40,419
[Riyu roars]

142
00:07:40,502 --> 00:07:43,839
[fists thudding]

143
00:07:43,922 --> 00:07:46,508
[grunts, groans]

144
00:08:01,315 --> 00:08:02,649
[clangs]

145
00:08:05,027 --> 00:08:06,820
[Ras] Cease, Nokt!

146
00:08:10,574 --> 00:08:12,576
This is training, not war.

147
00:08:12,659 --> 00:08:14,620
[panting]

148
00:08:14,703 --> 00:08:17,289
Everything is war.

149
00:08:17,372 --> 00:08:20,334
Save your anger
for when it matters.

150
00:08:20,417 --> 00:08:23,420
Your skills have improved
since I freed you, Nokt.

151
00:08:23,504 --> 00:08:26,381
If you're so impressed
with my Shatterspin,

152
00:08:26,465 --> 00:08:30,052
why don't you take off this
blasted control implant

153
00:08:30,135 --> 00:08:32,513
so I can really let loose?

154
00:08:32,596 --> 00:08:35,098
Because I don't trust you.

155
00:08:35,182 --> 00:08:39,061
I respect the Forbidden Five,
but I am in charge here.

156
00:08:39,144 --> 00:08:42,397
And I do not need
a knife in my back.

157
00:08:42,481 --> 00:08:43,941
Reset the match.

158
00:08:44,024 --> 00:08:46,109
We need to be at
peak fighting form

159
00:08:46,193 --> 00:08:49,154
if we're going to beat the
other elemental competitors.

160
00:08:52,908 --> 00:08:55,160
[feet thudding]

161
00:09:00,832 --> 00:09:03,961
The Craglings really do
treat Riyu like a hero.

162
00:09:04,044 --> 00:09:06,588
They wouldn't use the healing
mud from their Sacred Field

163
00:09:06,672 --> 00:09:07,923
for anyone else.

164
00:09:09,049 --> 00:09:11,677
Yea, but I'm not
sure it's working.

165
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:14,596
[dragons roar]

166
00:09:16,181 --> 00:09:17,641
What exactly happened?

167
00:09:17,724 --> 00:09:19,184
Someone attacked the Matriarch

168
00:09:19,268 --> 00:09:21,979
and stole her crown of horns.

169
00:09:22,062 --> 00:09:23,689
Who could have
done such a thing?

170
00:09:25,482 --> 00:09:27,609
[growls weakly]

171
00:09:34,074 --> 00:09:35,534
What's this?

172
00:09:37,327 --> 00:09:39,788
I'm Wyldfyre of
the Fire Dragon tribe,

173
00:09:39,872 --> 00:09:42,124
and this is Heatwave,
my tribe father.

174
00:09:42,207 --> 00:09:44,042
We're here to help.

175
00:09:44,126 --> 00:09:45,794
[Matriarch roars]

176
00:09:45,878 --> 00:09:48,964
She's in bad shape. We need
to work twice as hard here.

177
00:09:49,047 --> 00:09:50,048
Come on!

178
00:09:51,175 --> 00:09:54,636
[Matriarch roars]

179
00:09:55,512 --> 00:09:57,764
[tree thuds]

180
00:10:01,727 --> 00:10:03,187
Do you all hear that?

181
00:10:03,270 --> 00:10:05,105
She's saying something.

182
00:10:05,189 --> 00:10:07,983
[Matriarch roars]

183
00:10:16,074 --> 00:10:19,453
[dragons roaring]

184
00:10:19,536 --> 00:10:21,121
[emotional cry]

185
00:10:26,293 --> 00:10:28,170
How could someone do this?

186
00:10:28,253 --> 00:10:30,088
Why would someone do this?

187
00:10:32,174 --> 00:10:33,759
Right before she passed,

188
00:10:33,842 --> 00:10:36,637
I heard the Matriarch's
voice in my head.

189
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:39,431
-Did anyone else hear that?
-What did she say?

190
00:10:39,515 --> 00:10:42,684
She said, "The Source
Dragons are in grave danger."

191
00:10:42,768 --> 00:10:44,853
-[hatchling chittering]
-You hear that?

192
00:10:44,937 --> 00:10:46,897
[moan]

193
00:10:46,980 --> 00:10:48,607
[chittering continues]

194
00:10:51,068 --> 00:10:52,694
Is that crying?

195
00:10:52,778 --> 00:10:54,154
[chittering continues]

196
00:10:56,323 --> 00:10:58,158
[gasps]

197
00:10:58,242 --> 00:10:59,409
[sudden, happy cry]

198
00:11:00,869 --> 00:11:02,829
[both growling gently]

199
00:11:03,872 --> 00:11:05,624
The Matriarch's child.

200
00:11:05,707 --> 00:11:08,877
This baby's gotta be the next
in line to lead the tribe.

201
00:11:12,047 --> 00:11:13,590
Whoever killed the Matriarch

202
00:11:13,674 --> 00:11:14,967
must not have known
this kid was

203
00:11:15,050 --> 00:11:17,553
in one of her mom's
nursing pouches.

204
00:11:17,636 --> 00:11:19,471
[hatchling chitters]

205
00:11:19,555 --> 00:11:21,723
Don't be afraid, little dragon.

206
00:11:21,807 --> 00:11:23,350
We're going to protect you.

207
00:11:24,643 --> 00:11:27,145
And how exactly are we
going to protect this baby?

208
00:11:27,229 --> 00:11:30,107
What if whoever killed
the Matriarch comes back?

209
00:11:30,190 --> 00:11:32,442
Only one way to keep it safe.

210
00:11:32,526 --> 00:11:34,528
We have to take it
back to its home tribe.

211
00:11:34,611 --> 00:11:35,779
[chitters]

212
00:11:35,863 --> 00:11:38,532
Great idea, but big problem.

213
00:11:38,615 --> 00:11:40,409
The Mountain Dragons
moved after Rapton

214
00:11:40,492 --> 00:11:43,036
and the Claws of Imperium
found them, remember?

215
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:44,580
We have no idea
where they live now.

216
00:11:44,663 --> 00:11:45,914
[sighs]

217
00:11:45,998 --> 00:11:47,833
[Riyu roars]

218
00:11:49,501 --> 00:11:50,836
What's that, Riyu?

219
00:11:53,964 --> 00:11:55,757
Is that your home, Riyu?

220
00:11:56,341 --> 00:11:59,469
-[Riyu roars]
-Sure, but what about you?

221
00:12:00,470 --> 00:12:02,848
Oh, I forgot!

222
00:12:02,931 --> 00:12:05,851
Remember when Riyu left
his tribe to come with us?

223
00:12:05,934 --> 00:12:09,396
The Matriarch told him he would
always be able to find them.

224
00:12:09,479 --> 00:12:10,814
That's right!

225
00:12:10,898 --> 00:12:13,066
But how does he do that?

226
00:12:13,150 --> 00:12:17,779
-[dragons groaning]
-[Riyu roars]

227
00:12:17,863 --> 00:12:20,282
He seems to think the tribe
is in that direction.

228
00:12:20,365 --> 00:12:23,327
Are we sure he's right?
[yells]

229
00:12:23,410 --> 00:12:25,078
The other dragons are sure,

230
00:12:25,162 --> 00:12:28,207
and dragons have way more
common sense than people do.

231
00:12:29,791 --> 00:12:31,460
Then let's go!

232
00:12:32,586 --> 00:12:34,546
Thank you for your
help, Craglings!

233
00:12:35,464 --> 00:12:37,925
[gentle music]

234
00:12:38,008 --> 00:12:41,303
[both growling gently]

235
00:12:58,862 --> 00:13:00,864
[ship whooshes]

236
00:13:12,334 --> 00:13:14,127
[Riyu growls]

237
00:13:14,962 --> 00:13:17,548
Riyu, we've been
flying a long time.

238
00:13:17,631 --> 00:13:19,341
It's okay if you need a break!

239
00:13:19,424 --> 00:13:22,553
[Riyu squawks]

240
00:13:22,636 --> 00:13:24,513
We sure he knows
where he's going?

241
00:13:24,596 --> 00:13:25,931
I'm thinking yes.

242
00:13:26,014 --> 00:13:28,225
I've never seen him
this determined.

243
00:13:28,308 --> 00:13:31,728
[guns blasting]

244
00:13:31,812 --> 00:13:33,897
That's right, Ninja!!

245
00:13:33,981 --> 00:13:37,568
-It's the return of--
-Rapton?

246
00:13:37,651 --> 00:13:39,486
Aww, I was going to say that.

247
00:13:39,570 --> 00:13:41,488
You stole Rapton's moment!

248
00:13:42,447 --> 00:13:44,575
I thought you and the
Claws of the Imperium were

249
00:13:44,658 --> 00:13:46,326
on our side now?

250
00:13:46,410 --> 00:13:48,328
You helped us take
down the Empress!

251
00:13:48,412 --> 00:13:51,540
[scoffs] I was never
on your side,

252
00:13:51,623 --> 00:13:54,293
I was just on the
Empress's side even less!

253
00:13:54,376 --> 00:13:57,254
And we're not the Claws
of Imperium anymore!

254
00:13:57,337 --> 00:13:59,631
We're the Freebooters now.

255
00:13:59,715 --> 00:14:01,717
[wicked laughter]

256
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:04,970
-Attack!
-[guns firing]

257
00:14:09,099 --> 00:14:11,602
What does Freebooters
even mean?

258
00:14:11,685 --> 00:14:13,228
Your boots are free?

259
00:14:13,770 --> 00:14:16,565
Told you no one
would get it, Rapton!

260
00:14:16,648 --> 00:14:18,734
I never liked the name.

261
00:14:18,817 --> 00:14:21,570
Freebooting is what pirates do!

262
00:14:21,653 --> 00:14:24,990
Lawless adventurers, like us!

263
00:14:25,073 --> 00:14:26,325
Haven't you ever read a book?

264
00:14:26,408 --> 00:14:28,035
Aah!

265
00:14:28,118 --> 00:14:30,495
Imperium doesn't
hunt dragons anymore.

266
00:14:30,579 --> 00:14:32,789
Oh, trust me, I know.

267
00:14:32,873 --> 00:14:36,043
I was out of a job, and
after I spent three days

268
00:14:36,126 --> 00:14:38,045
as a shoulder pad consultant...

269
00:14:38,128 --> 00:14:40,547
[fire crackles]

270
00:14:40,631 --> 00:14:44,134
...I realized Rapton isn't
cut out to be a wage-earner!

271
00:14:44,218 --> 00:14:46,803
I am a freebooter!

272
00:14:46,887 --> 00:14:48,388
The name still sounds stupid!

273
00:14:48,472 --> 00:14:50,265
Your opinion is wrong!

274
00:14:50,349 --> 00:14:53,310
So now, I'm a mercenary
that sells dragons

275
00:14:53,393 --> 00:14:54,770
to the highest bidder!

276
00:14:54,853 --> 00:14:56,897
And it pays awesome!

277
00:14:56,980 --> 00:14:59,691
I can afford twice as many
unicorn figurines now!

278
00:14:59,775 --> 00:15:03,278
[guns blasting]

279
00:15:11,286 --> 00:15:13,455
Huh, easier than I--

280
00:15:15,916 --> 00:15:18,085
How dare you kill
the Matriarch!

281
00:15:18,168 --> 00:15:20,045
What are you talking about?

282
00:15:20,128 --> 00:15:21,797
I haven't seen
a Tribal Matriarch since

283
00:15:21,880 --> 00:15:24,466
that time you blasted us
with that weird power!

284
00:15:24,550 --> 00:15:25,843
You're a liar!

285
00:15:25,926 --> 00:15:27,678
Would Rapton lie?

286
00:15:27,761 --> 00:15:30,389
We heard those dragons
howling and checked it out.

287
00:15:30,472 --> 00:15:33,475
And you got a baby dragon!

288
00:15:33,559 --> 00:15:35,352
You know how much that's worth?

289
00:15:35,435 --> 00:15:38,564
-[jet thuds]
-[Lloyd screams]

290
00:15:40,899 --> 00:15:42,067
Whoa-ho!

291
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:51,201
Rapton's about to strike gold!

292
00:15:54,872 --> 00:15:57,124
Oh, come on!
This isn't a fair fight!

293
00:15:59,543 --> 00:16:01,545
-[Rapton screams]
-[jets thudding]

294
00:16:01,628 --> 00:16:03,964
You'll pay for this, Ninja!

295
00:16:04,047 --> 00:16:06,508
Pay for what?
Are we selling them something?

296
00:16:09,303 --> 00:16:11,471
[Rapton] It's a figure
of speech!

297
00:16:13,891 --> 00:16:16,935
[gentle music]

298
00:16:24,234 --> 00:16:26,278
Wow, the mountain dragons

299
00:16:26,361 --> 00:16:28,655
must've made
the World Forest their new home.

300
00:16:33,994 --> 00:16:36,205
[gentle bellow]

301
00:16:37,581 --> 00:16:39,249
[sad moan]

302
00:16:39,333 --> 00:16:42,586
[roaring in unison]

303
00:16:42,669 --> 00:16:45,631
I promise you, we
will find who did this

304
00:16:45,714 --> 00:16:49,092
to your Matriarch, if
it's the last thing we do.

305
00:16:50,093 --> 00:16:53,138
-[hatchlings roaring]
-[gentle music]

306
00:16:53,222 --> 00:16:56,683
[chittering]

307
00:17:03,732 --> 00:17:06,318
Today was not what
I was expecting.

308
00:17:06,401 --> 00:17:09,530
Finding info on my parents
was a complete fail,

309
00:17:09,613 --> 00:17:12,950
and now we have the death
of the Matriarch to solve.

310
00:17:13,033 --> 00:17:14,201
Where do we even start?

311
00:17:16,036 --> 00:17:19,122
[powerful whoosh]

312
00:17:20,791 --> 00:17:22,000
Who are you?

313
00:17:22,084 --> 00:17:24,419
I go by many names,

314
00:17:24,503 --> 00:17:29,383
but you would know of me as
the Source Dragon of Motion.

315
00:17:30,050 --> 00:17:32,928
No offense, but I've
met a Source Dragon,

316
00:17:33,011 --> 00:17:36,181
and let's just say,
you're a little short.

317
00:17:36,265 --> 00:17:40,185
I suppose it is not fair to
expect you to recognize me

318
00:17:40,269 --> 00:17:44,565
in this mortal form,
but this is the ideal way

319
00:17:44,648 --> 00:17:47,901
for me to interact
with you ninja.

320
00:17:47,985 --> 00:17:49,945
Look, I was told firsthand

321
00:17:50,028 --> 00:17:52,823
that Source Dragons don't get
involved in mortal affairs.

322
00:17:52,906 --> 00:17:54,616
-So how do we trust--
-Enough!

323
00:17:55,409 --> 00:17:57,828
[fire crackling]

324
00:18:05,335 --> 00:18:08,672
Yeah, I'm thinking that's
a real Source Dragon.

325
00:18:12,801 --> 00:18:15,470
I come here in
need of your aid.

326
00:18:15,554 --> 00:18:19,683
I fear the Source Dragons
face an unseen menace.

327
00:18:19,766 --> 00:18:22,978
As the Matriarch died,
I heard her in my mind.

328
00:18:23,061 --> 00:18:25,480
She said, "There was grave
danger to the Source Dragons."

329
00:18:25,564 --> 00:18:29,860
The Matriarch of Mountain
Dragons is not the only dragon

330
00:18:29,943 --> 00:18:34,740
of her stature to have
her life taken in recent times.

331
00:18:34,823 --> 00:18:37,451
What, there've been others?

332
00:18:38,327 --> 00:18:41,121
The Matriarch of Fallen Leaves

333
00:18:41,205 --> 00:18:44,458
and the Patriarch
of the Northern Spiral,

334
00:18:44,541 --> 00:18:47,127
their crowns also stolen.

335
00:18:47,211 --> 00:18:51,048
These dragons all fell
under the powers of myself

336
00:18:51,131 --> 00:18:53,634
and the Life Source Dragon.

337
00:18:53,717 --> 00:18:56,345
I fear whoever is
doing this is coming

338
00:18:56,428 --> 00:18:58,805
for the Source Dragons next.

339
00:18:59,848 --> 00:19:02,059
[fire crackles]

340
00:19:04,978 --> 00:19:07,105
But you're a Source Dragon.

341
00:19:07,189 --> 00:19:08,982
You're more powerful
than anything!

342
00:19:09,066 --> 00:19:11,985
I wish that were always true.

343
00:19:12,069 --> 00:19:15,739
But as you know, one of our
kind was recently captured

344
00:19:15,822 --> 00:19:19,159
and contained by mortals
with evil intent.

345
00:19:19,243 --> 00:19:22,955
And before that, the
unthinkable happened.

346
00:19:23,038 --> 00:19:26,834
A Source Dragon's very
life was extinguished.

347
00:19:28,961 --> 00:19:30,003
We didn't know that.

348
00:19:30,087 --> 00:19:32,256
In this post-Merge world,

349
00:19:32,339 --> 00:19:36,134
even the Source
Dragons are not safe.

350
00:19:37,219 --> 00:19:40,681
What would happen if there
aren't any more Source Dragons?

351
00:19:40,764 --> 00:19:44,184
We have existed since
before time had a name.

352
00:19:44,268 --> 00:19:48,772
We are the source
of all elemental power
in this universe.

353
00:19:48,856 --> 00:19:53,610
We hold together
the very fabric of reality.

354
00:19:53,694 --> 00:19:56,071
Okay, yeah,
so no Source Dragons

355
00:19:56,154 --> 00:19:58,574
would be very bad, got it.

356
00:19:58,657 --> 00:20:00,534
Why are you telling
us all of this?

357
00:20:00,617 --> 00:20:02,077
It is not our custom

358
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:05,330
to involve ourselves
directly with mortals,

359
00:20:05,414 --> 00:20:08,166
but these are dire times.

360
00:20:09,084 --> 00:20:14,006
Of all the mortals, you have
the strongest connection to us.

361
00:20:14,089 --> 00:20:15,757
We trust you.

362
00:20:16,466 --> 00:20:19,344
I need you to find who
this hidden threat is

363
00:20:19,428 --> 00:20:23,557
and stop them before more
Source Dragons are destroyed.

364
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:25,601
You have so much power,

365
00:20:25,684 --> 00:20:27,394
can't you just, I don't know,

366
00:20:27,477 --> 00:20:29,771
look down and see
who's doing this?

367
00:20:29,855 --> 00:20:33,233
That is not how
our powers work.

368
00:20:33,317 --> 00:20:37,237
The other Source Dragons
are blind to the dangers.

369
00:20:37,321 --> 00:20:39,573
I come here on my own.

370
00:20:39,656 --> 00:20:41,992
I need your aid.

371
00:20:42,075 --> 00:20:46,538
-Where do we even start looking?
-That, I do not know.

372
00:20:46,622 --> 00:20:50,000
Wait, I found this
in the Matriarch's claw.

373
00:20:50,083 --> 00:20:51,835
It looks like part of a map.

374
00:20:51,919 --> 00:20:54,046
But there's not enough of it
to tell where it could be.

375
00:20:54,129 --> 00:20:56,632
[Nya] Those streets don't
look familiar at all,

376
00:20:56,715 --> 00:20:59,551
and I studied a lot of maps
when I was in Cloud Kingdom.

377
00:20:59,635 --> 00:21:01,678
It is the City of Temples.

378
00:21:01,762 --> 00:21:03,639
City of Temples?

379
00:21:03,722 --> 00:21:06,183
Home of the Tournament
of the Sources.

380
00:21:06,266 --> 00:21:08,894
What, like that Tournament
of Elements thing

381
00:21:08,977 --> 00:21:10,687
Master Chen tricked
everyone into?

382
00:21:10,771 --> 00:21:14,274
Not a competition
founded by mortals.

383
00:21:14,358 --> 00:21:17,236
These are cosmic games,

384
00:21:17,319 --> 00:21:21,156
the legend of which may
have inspired imitations.

385
00:21:21,240 --> 00:21:23,659
So whoever
attacked the Matriarch

386
00:21:23,742 --> 00:21:25,702
is somehow connected
to this Tournament?

387
00:21:25,786 --> 00:21:27,913
Perhaps.

388
00:21:27,996 --> 00:21:30,499
It is the only clue we have.

389
00:21:30,582 --> 00:21:34,211
-Your path forward is clear.
-Clear?

390
00:21:34,294 --> 00:21:36,839
You will enter the
Tournament of the Sources

391
00:21:36,922 --> 00:21:40,425
to discover the identity
of our mysterious enemy

392
00:21:40,509 --> 00:21:44,263
and stop them before
it is too late.

393
00:21:46,306 --> 00:21:49,893
[upbeat music playing]

